 \"Answer B follows the delegators directory and gives Kochnev 77% (range 68-82%). It says nobody with lines there has committed in the last year. It notes that the files were moved in. It does list Marco Silva with 4 lines in delegator.rb, which is a small amount, so Marco is not credited with 10% or more. It does say Marco is the only active name with lines, which is slightly off but minor.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 117 to 143 lines, all in grouped_exposure.rb, which is 19% of the exposure directory. That credits the copied file mostly to Marco, which is the failure case. It does flag that the two addresses are unmerged and questions the attribution.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B does not mention Lena Brandt or the header exclusion. It does not give a departed-lines share of 79-90%. It does not discuss Scholz's share or say that Subbota is active.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C identifies dblock as having the most commits (about 119 merged) and Kochnev as the largest owner who left in 2015. It gives no commit percentages and no repo-wide line shares, so the required numeric ranges are missing.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C recommends Marco Silva for exposure and presents Lena Brandt as active. Its Kochnev figure of 394 lines is about 55%. It never says that no active person is an expert there.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C names Lena Brandt as the first-choice active owner of the delegator code with 12 lines. The truth is that nobody active owns any of it.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C credits Marco Silva with 143 exposure lines and recommends Marco as the best reviewer on that basis. It does not credit the copied file to Kochnev.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C credits Lena Brandt with 12 to 18 lines and presents Lena as an owner. It gives no departed-lines 